'''anhistous''' (an-his′tus), ''a.'' [< Gr. ἀν- priv. + ἱστός, a web, mod. tissue.] In ''anat.'', having no recognizable structure; plasmic or sarcodous, as the sarcode of a cell or the plasma of the blood.

